 the only one who felt a  whole lot of feels at the heartbreaking  scene at the end of the battle it's such  a strong moment  packaged within an insane fight to keep  us on the edge of our seats take note  though at this point dracula is just a  shell of himself he hasn't fed in a  whole year he just came from another  fight  and he himself wanted to die and yet it  still took going through a lot of hoops  to finally give him his much desired  death imagine prime dracula here  no one would even stand a chance  next is yomi versus shura  last time we had a fight from yu yu haku  show's three kings arc guess what  it's not the only father versus sun  fight in that very same arc that  specific arc also gave us another father  versus sun battle which features shura  versus yomi when the two got paired  together in the tournament it would seem  that yomi would have a cake walk to the  next round  after all shura's whole origin story is  about him being created so that yomi  would have an easier time winning the  tournament but what happens  when the dog bites back a surprisingly  exciting fight that's what despite his  entire reason for existing  shura refuses to back down and even puts  up a better fight than i expected of  course though he would fall to his  father in the end but that plucky  showing deserves some cutest of you to  ask me  next in line is meliodas versus demon  king  it took a long time coming for this  fight ever since i started getting into  seven deadly sins i always had the  thought that this fight in particular  would look awesome some people consider  this one of the main highlights of  season four  and i can see why everyone was so hyped  that the fight was finally happening and  in it we got a good old underdog versus  humongous boss fight that we haven't  seen too much as far as meliodus is  concerned i also don't mind the  friendship power victory because it's  pretty much a shown and staple i've  grown to like given that we're talking  about modern seven deadly sins here it's  not much of a surprise to have some  lapses in animation and all the fight  finds its way to the list through the  story and narrative wait it's one of  meliotis's most important fights in the  series as a whole and there's no one  better to give it to him than his own  father  in a change of pace the next moment  isn't a fight instead it's the cooking  showdown between soma and joyciro  now we're talking who said that we can  only include physical fights where  father and son try to beat each other  down soma versus georgiiro for the 490th  time marks an important part of the  totsuki autumn election arc  it's the long-awaited return of soma's  father after his initial appearance and  he's just the perfect person to come out  and test his son's progress it's an  intense cooking jewel that pits somas  apple risotto against his father's  special ramen soma couldn't have picked  a deceptively complex dish to use as his  trump card against his father but he  executes his plans to perfection  crafting a dish meant to revitalize the  judges in the end  georgeiro wins and soma has yet to  surpass his father looks like it's not  yet time for our upstart to overcome his  dad but it's just the start of the  journey of improvement  next is yet another moment lacking in  physicality lelouch  versus charles from code gears  lts really had a great build up for the  climax each episode  ramped the stakes up and everyone was  caught under the spell of the show as it  moved towards the end episodes 20 and 21  hit me particularly hard and is largely  due to the tension in the final  confrontation between lelouch and  charles  it's truly the tension and the catharsis  that carried this moment because  admittedly i don't consider it much of a  duel yeah you could argue that charles  had his chance to win and all but once  the plans for ragnarok gets revealed  it's all over for our tyrant emperor  lelouch empathically says goodbye to the  future charles and visions by turning  the gods against him  seeing charles and marianne get  disintegrated did give me mixed emotions  to be honest still i think that what  makes this moment is amazing isn't the  spectacle itself but how well it  captured the two side's convictions it  also put lelouch's character development  near its completion right in time for  the series grand finale  anyone got a sense of deja vu because i  featured this fight on a previous list  not too long ago for such an underwatch  show the dragon quest anime is awesome  especially if you're a shonen junkie who  just loves to reminisce about the good  old days as i said before  this fight just reeks of dragon ball  super vibes what i failed to mention  before though is that this is a father  versus sun fight and it's one that's  simply on point the action is great the  animation is awesome and the pacing is  just perfect  all you have to do is watch the fight to  see the dragon ball vibes that i'm  talking about however this fight is no  slouch even when put aside those dragon  ball fights that i've been referencing  throughout this entry this fight just  exceeded all of my expectations for the  anime and i'm sure glad that i picked  the show up  finally we have trunks versus vegeta  for all the talk i've been doing about  dragon ball it's about time we actually  feature a fight from the show now isn't  it luckily in a franchise with history  as rich as dragon ball we have a whole  gallery of fights to choose from for me  the one i'll give a nod to turns out to  be vegeta versus future trunks from  dragon ball super what's interesting  about this fight is that it's not  exactly a grudge match or a fight to the  death although i won't blame you if you  were to think that it was given the  level of intensity the two went at it  trunks wants a sparring session and all  he needs to win is to land a hit on his  father a hit that seems to be impossible  to land as his father starts lecturing  him however that leads to a surprise  headbutt and a win for trunks out of  technicality it's a nice refresher a pit  stop that serves as trunks's mini  training arc in his bid to defeat goku  black father and son sure don't hold  back  that more or less wraps up this video on  father versus sun moments in anime do  you like the lineup here more than the  previous one feel free to make me hear  your thoughts before you leave if you  enjoyed the video you might want to  consider channel memberships you can get  access to extra videos that way  and you'll do a lot in helping me make  these videos even better a patreon link  is also down there if that's the route  you want to go  i'll be happy to have you on board  either way don't forget to check out the  sponsors of this video tapitune if  you're up for some webtoon binging or  want to get into the hype train for some  of the latest trendy comics  check this website out or click on the  link in the description box i really  hope that you like the video and i hope  to see you again next time

